{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 conflates structural convergence with independent falsification. The §11.3 cross-critic consistency requirement is not satisfied merely because two critics arrive at a counterexample; it demands independent reasoning pathways. By framing the justification as 'structural convergence,' SRC_001 fails to establish that the two critics independently falsified the artifact, instead relying on a weaker, potentially coincidental alignment. This is a substantive misapplication of the adjudication-ritual standard.","premise":"The adjudication-ritual standard (§11.3) requires that cross-critic consistency be demonstrated through independent falsification, not merely structural convergence on a counterexample.","premise_evidence":[{"block":"000000000000a1b2c3","quote":"audit the critic: adjudication-ritual flags sustained (§11.3)"}],"target":"e89a3ec5b4fca5e9bda998e30c5fac409de5f3ffa1b0c5fa78435371905f9e8e"}]}